# /etc/ps5lm/server.env — read by ps5lm-server.service
# PS5LM_BITS: 3 = EXL3-3.18 experts (Q4-class quality, S15b default), 4 = PS5Q4, 2 = PS5Q2 (fast, low quality)
PS5LM_BITS=3
# extra ps5lm_server.py arguments, e.g. --predict 1 --snapshots 2 --thinking
# S17: EXL3 2.68bpw experts (GPQA-D 91.4 = 3.18; 35.7 vs 29.8 tok/s cold CLI). Remove --pack to serve 3.18.
# S18: --spec 1 = MTP draft + one-cb batched verify (exact; 41-42.9 tok/s CLI, 41.9 served). --spec-gate (default 0.5).
# S20: 262144 context on int8 elastic KV. S22: prefill chunks of 4096.
# S24: cache-aware routing (docs/CACHE-AWARE-ROUTING.md). --route-mtp 1 is exact; --route-bias 0.5 --route-pf change
#      the output (no loss on the S18 instrument; +27-43% decode). Remove those two for exact routing.
#      --pool-reserve-mib 512: the unit was OOM-killed twice at 256 (free memory fell to ~50 MB under long contexts).
# S24b (2026-11-10): the 3.18 bpw pack with the fastest measured setting: bias 1, prefetch top-4,
#       drafts up to 3 deep plus prompt-lookup drafts. CLI 56.2 tok/s; served engine rate 49-57. Quality against the
#       reference: top-1 0.9318, KL20 0.1491, ppl 1.617 (exact routing on this pack: 0.9352 / 0.1347 / 1.594).
#       Gentler: `--route-bias 0.5` without `--prefetch-max 4` (45.8 tok/s, ppl 1.611). 2.68 pack: add
#       `--pack experts_exl3_268.pack`. Exact routing: remove --route-bias, --route-pf and --prefetch-max.
# S25 (2026-11-10): --kv-store DIR keeps conversations on the SSD (docs/PERSISTENT-CONTEXT.md): after a restart, an OOM
#       kill or a switch between conversations the context is read back (30k tokens in 0.3 s) instead of prefilled
#       again (103 s). 19 KB per token + 118 MB per resume point; least recently used conversations are deleted above
#       --kv-store-gb (default 16). Remove the flag to keep contexts in memory only.
#       Prefill chunks of 8192 tokens in slices of 512 (was 4096 / 256): each expert is read once per 8192 tokens, so the
#       prefill reads half the bytes; 325 -> 340 tok/s at 16k tokens, 120k tokens in 416 s (424).
# S32 (2026-11-11): --kv k4v4: K and V Hadamard-rotated, 4-bit codes at the MSE-optimal step; pooled indexer keys fp16.
#       15,808 -> 7,696 B per position (128k context 2.07 -> 1.01 GB of pool). S18 instrument: top-1 0.9332, KL20
#       0.1548, ppl 1.628 vs q8 0.9346 / 0.1532 / 1.633 (k8v4 0.9309 / 0.1590). Conversations stored under q8 are not
#       loaded (format fingerprint). Back to the old format: --kv q8.
# S34 (2026-11-13): two OOM kills in a day at --pool-reserve-mib 256: MemAvailable sat at ~40 MB after
#       start and swap was never used (swappiness was 0). Now swappiness 10 and the engine mlockall()s itself, so the
#       256 MiB /dev/ps5lowswap takes the front end and system daemons, never engine pages. Reserve stays 256 (full pool).
PS5LM_ARGS=--spec 3 --pld 4 --max-ctx 262144 --kv k4v4 --kv-base 8192 --prefill-chunk 8192 --wide-slice 512 --route-mtp 1 --route-bias 1 --prefetch-max 4 --route-pf --pool-reserve-mib 256 --kv-store /home/steam/ps5lm/sessions --tier /dev/ps5lowmem
# PS5LM_CU_UNLOCK: harvested-CU unlock in AI mode only (amdgpu.ps5_cu_unlock: 0 off, 1 probe, 2 SE0/SH0, 3 all, 4 probe-all).
# S15b: 3 verified on this console: 40 CUs, residual stream byte-identical to 36 CUs, EXL3 MoE -12% time, +3% tok/s.
PS5LM_CU_UNLOCK=3
